// Differential tests for uos/rt/gzip.hpp. Every expected outcome below was recorded from Bun 1.4.0
// by scratch scripts (not kept) and is embedded as JSON:
// - recipes: the deterministic inputs both sides build (sizes, SHA-256, and the size and SHA-256 of
//   Bun's CompressionStream("gzip") output for comparison);
// - ours: gzipSync's output for every recipe, which Bun's DecompressionStream inflated back to the
//   recipe (SHA-256 checked), with the pieces Bun's reader got for several input chunkings. The
//   SHA-256 of gzipSync's bytes is pinned: another libz may write other (valid) bytes, and then
//   these vectors must be re-recorded;
// - streams: DecompressionStream("gzip" | "deflate" | "deflate-raw") over one Blob (well-formed,
//   multi-member, every gzip header field, corrupt, truncated, trailing data, other formats):
//   the pieces read and the rejection (name, message, code);
// - chunked: the same over explicit ReadableStream chunks (member and stream boundaries between
//   chunks, byte by byte, 100-byte chunks of 1 MiB of zeros);
// - foreign: gzip streams from Bun's CompressionStream and node:zlib (levels 0/1/9, filtered,
//   Huffman-only, RLE and fixed strategies, memLevel 1/9, 9- and 12-bit windows, every header
//   field, three members) that gunzipSync must inflate;
// - fetch: what Bun's fetch returned for Content-Encoding gzip / x-gzip / deflate bodies from a
//   loopback server: the trailing policies reproduce it (the decoding rule is in docs/rt/gzip.md).
// Links: tests/rt/gzip_test.cpp (every src/rt/*.cpp links automatically).
